IoT Fundamentals
Change the Logic




before
if (digitalRead(7) == LOW) {
  digitalWrite(4, HIGH);
}




after
if (digitalRead(7) == LOW) {
  digitalWrite(4, LOW);
}

Challenge: make the LED turn OFF when pressed, or ON when released — whichever is the opposite of what you built. Change only the code.

Did the wiring need to change at all?
No — the circuit is identical. Only the decision in code c

IoT Fundamentals
Modify the Counter




sketch.ino
if (count % 3 == 0) {
  blinkLED();
}

Challenge: make the LED blink after every third press.
Same wiring, same counter — only the reaction to the count changes.

IoT Fundamentals
Change the Logic




before
if (detected) {
  digitalWrite(LED, HIGH);
}




after
if (detected) {
  digitalWrite(LED, LOW);
}

LED ON when detected → change it so LED OFF when detected, ON otherwise.

Key idea: hardware can stay the same while program logic changes.
